BR>29. Air fresheners can’t hide the fact that this is a smoker’s car. The smell is still there<BR>30. Cigarette burn on driver’s seat (on left rib cage support)<BR>31. Windshield tint is faded There is stress on the windshield. Will hold for now but abrupt climate changes will make it it break. Windshield $130 tint $25<P>how much do you think it is worth?<BR>I calculate that to get the car properly running it would cost $1300 (tranny, cv axle and radiator)<P>please post even if you are not sure how much it would cost. I need opinions. Lots of opinions. thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||ferg||06-05-2001||12:38 PM||||I'd almost sell you mine for $4000, and it doesn't need any of that (it's not for sale)<P>Not seeing the car, it sounds really rough. I've always heard when estimating how much something will cost, take what you think it will take to fix and multiply it by 2. But you've seen this car and I haven't and you didn't say what your plans are for it- i.e. fully restored, kit car, total custom, etc.<P>I personally wouldn't give the guy anything more than $2000, and if I saw the car I might not give that much for it. <P>I've seen quite a few fiero's out there for near that price that are in much better shape. <P>Obviously, I don't know your situation, but for my money I'd rather spend more money up front for a better car vs. buying a car with problems for an average price.<P>take a look at this.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.auto-rv.com/browser.asp?ADName=CI9080315" TARGET=_blank>http://www.auto-rv.com/browser.asp?ADName=CI9080315</A> <P>Yeah it's 2x the asking price of the one you're looking at, and it's not a v-8, but- it doesn't look like it needs anything so you can spend your time driving it, rather than fixing it. <P>BTW- this car would be approx 3-4 hours from you.<p>[This message has been edited by ferg (edited 06-05-2001).]||||reg||1
